task id=1 status=todo {
    title "Initialize project from starter template"
    created "2026-03-14T17:11:47.551455+00:00"
    modified "2026-10-20T09:51:39+00:00"
    description #"""
Run in a clone of a new repository created through GitHub's "Use this template"
action. Default the project slug to the current repository directory name;
use the existing origin as the destination.

1. Inspect repository guidance, Git status, history, and origin's fetch and push
   URLs before making changes. Verify this is the generated project's clone,
   not the source template or an already initialized project. Preserve unrelated
   work, Git history, and remotes; never reset history or force-push.
2. Identify the template's old name from the root package.json. Replace every
   occurrence of that name, case-insensitively, with the new project slug or
   display name throughout repository-owned files, including hidden files,
   documentation, configuration, package metadata, URLs, and task instructions.
   Rename any paths containing the old name too. Exclude Git internals,
   dependencies, generated output, and external URLs identifying dependencies.
3. Update README.md: replace template clone/setup instructions with project
   documentation, the new title, and the new development and preview URLs.
4. Update AGENTS.md: describe the new project and update local URLs. Keep
   CLAUDE.md as a reference to the shared guidance.
5. Update client/index.html: set the title, description, and Open Graph title
   and description. Only set deployment URLs and social images when known;
   do not invent a production domain or asset.
6. Update the root package.json name (lowercase/hyphenated), and client/package.json
   portless dev/preview routes to <name> and <name>-preview. Preserve other flags.
7. Check client/playwright.config.ts for old project URLs. Preserve a generic
   localhost test URL when it intentionally bypasses portless for CI.
8. Search all repository-owned files and paths again for the old name and
   resolve remaining occurrences. Install dependencies using the lockfile,
   then run lint, unit tests, production build, and end-to-end tests. If the
   default test port is occupied, use PLAYWRIGHT_PORT with an available port.
9. Record initialization as complete, stage the initialization changes, and
   commit on main with the message "Initialize project", preserving the existing
   commits. Push with git push -u origin main.
10. Verify the remote main commit matches local HEAD and the working tree is clean.
"""#
}
